{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1475331-the-tarpan-wastes-an-exalted-essence-actual-play","id":1475331,"title":"The Tarpan Wastes - An Exalted Essence Actual Play","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-02-23T10:16:41-08:00","id":1475331,"title":"The Tarpan Wastes - An Exalted Essence Actual Play","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">After talking about Exalted: Essence for several months, my group was finally in a position for me to run a game of it. Most of the group has experience with Exalted 3rd Edition (I ran a Solars game shortly after the Core book dropped that went all the way up to Essence 5 that was a lot of fun, and a second game that got kinda killed by real-life and COVID), with only my husband being new to the system.</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The pitch for the game was the following:</span></span></span></span><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Among barren plains, vast fields of weathered stone, and the lifeless salt flats of the Tarpan Wastes, it is easy to disappear.<br /> <br /> Or at least, it was. Where once a blind eye was turned, now all too many are beginning to peer into the Wastes, as a newly ascended dragon, an ancient doomsday cult, and a cruel new goddess with Immaculate sanction all begin to exert their influence.<br /> <br /> <br /> Enter the Circle...<br /> <br /> ------<br /> <br /> Gentle winters, long growing seasons, immense amounts of wealth, and more, all give the Blessed Isle its moniker. The stabilizing presence of the Pole of Earth helps inhabitants of the Isle live long, healthy lives, even for the peasant class.<br /> <br /> But not so for the Tarpan Wastes\u2014once among the lushest on the Isle, the ancient magics granting it vitality began to weaken centuries ago, and eventually failed. Unable to restore these complex workings and enchantments, nearly all left the Wastes as the crops died and wells dried up. Now only a sparse few hardy folk live in this desert, while criminals and dispossessed hide among the rocks and sand, all in the shadow of the Trigram Monastery.<br /> <br /> Tharasht Tears-of-Dust, the desert\u2019s cruel new goddess, has Immaculate sanction and plans to enforce their (and her) will among the scattered rebellious gods of the region. Meanwhile, Splendid Cinder, a recently enlightened elemental dragon, is founding their new court among the local spirits and is sure to come in conflict with Tharasht\u2019s machinations. All this while rumors are growing of a new cult in the region, where blessings of stone and safety come with proclamations of imminent doom.</div> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">We did character creation across last December, taking full advantage of the variety of Exalt types available in Essence, and started playing in the new year, with a bit of a cold-open with a *heavily* modified Tomb of Dreams conversion. I fully intend to keep this updated as I know that I always poke around for actual plays when I am starting a new game, so I figure other people might as well.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The Cast:</span></span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Steel Bane in the Dreams of the Dead (aka Dreams), Day Caste Abyssal - Very stabby, with a pair of artifact sais and a familiar</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The Duke of Endless Tears (aka The Duke), Midnight Caste Abyssal - Necromancer-Priest Horseman (unfortunately, he had to bow out after the initial arc due to RL)</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Swims through Raindrops (aka Rain), Casteless Lunar - Protective and friends/allies with Won Shik, spirit-shape of a great, protective brown bear</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Tepet Navar, Eclipse Caste Solar - Sorcerer and Craftsman, coming to terms with exalting as an Anathema</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Won Shik, Summer Caste Getimian - Martial Artist/</span>Musician who not only doesn't recognize the Creation that he awoke to, but was also thrown centuries into the future</li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Diyu Yor, Ascendant Caste Infernal - Gunslinging Anarchist who greatly enjoys his intoxicants</span></li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">And now for the session recaps!</span></span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}